{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From the top of the rocks I see him.</b> For he was on the height, and it is high. And the proof for \"the height\" is as I explained, and he did not go time after time to meet Nahashim, and he turned his face toward the wilderness and not toward the height. Also possible: \"from the top of the rocks\" is a metaphor for the decrees that descend from the supernal ones, for he saw in his wisdom that this nation would stand alone and not intermingle with others — overpowering [any nation] that would [try] to make it abandon its Torah, as all the nations did." "<b>And among the nations it is not reckoned.</b> I will explain it in [the comment on] the verse יָצֵב גְּבֻלֹת עַמִּים [\"He established the boundaries of peoples\"], Deuteronomy 32:8."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The suffix in לבד' is resolved as standalone 'alone'; could also read as לבדו 'on its own'."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:08.345140998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}